Python executation process is more complex than c and assembly because python do not interact with the cpu directly.

Python uses a Python virtual machine in order to convert the byte instructions to machine code.

Python code firstly get tokenised, during this process the python code is broken down into smaller pieces called tokens.

After tokenization, Python parses those tokens and creates a structure representing the code, commonly understood as an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST). This process also checks whether the code follows Python's grammar and syntax rules.

Then code is complied to byte code which is executed by PVM.

The main point which we need to keep in mind is that PVM is a python intreperter, which in most of the cases is Cpython and it is written in C language. Therefore, PVM is simply complied code of C language which is used for executing the byte code. 
